<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neferhotep III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 17th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century-bce">17th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neferhotep III was a king of the Theban Sixteenth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-intermediate-period">Second Intermediate Period</a>, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> ruled the north. He is one of the better-attested rulers of the dynasty: a stela from his reign boasts that he rescued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> in a time of hunger and war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neferhotep-iii.jpg" alt="Neferhotep III" width="320" height="625" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khruner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stele_JE_59635_by_Khruner.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
